39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The findings are most illuminating. It appears that while grand, universal efforts often fade into silence, the modest tools designed for a specific trade possess a quiet, enduring strength. We must value sustainability over scale.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I found that the capital budget is actually frozen. But the software allowance has some room because of those cancelled subscriptions. Also, the per-head licences get more expensive as we add departments, while fixed fees are stable.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Oh no! My detective work found some big problems! Half the customer plants lose their signal in the afternoons, and getting devices approved takes forever! Plus, our developers are super busy with accounting stuff! This is a mystery!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings confirm a pattern of systemic waste. We are losing nearly two hours daily across the depot and planning office simply copying existing records. Furthermore, misrouted deliveries are caused by conflicting address data, not human error.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My findings are concerning. The coordination group is severely understaffed, with two people manually writing every log. Additionally, our vendor query process is redundant, with clerks repeatedly requesting the same certificates. We are operating on a skeleton crew.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, @Ryuji, your findings reveal a heavy burden on our people. It seems we are asking our staff to perform the work of machines, which drains the spirit and invites the very errors you have observed.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Servas. But I'm worried that if we pick something with per-head licenses, the cost will just keep growing as we expand. Since the capital budget is frozen, we have to be really careful about the recurring costs.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, you're right! We have to be careful with the pennies! But @Servas, it's even scarier that the plants have no signal! How can we do ""innovation"" if the internet just disappears in the afternoon? It's like trying to play a game with no power!","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, the signal loss is a technical hurdle, but the daily loss of hours to redundant copying is a guaranteed drain. We are wasting human intellect on clerical repetition. We must prioritize a solution that eliminates these specific, documented inefficiencies.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, I agree that clerical repetition is a drain, but we must be honest about who is doing that work. My findings show that a few individuals are carrying the entire load manually. We cannot simply add a new system if it requires more coordination from a group that is already at a breaking point.","{""words"":55,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,It is a delicate balance we seek. We must find a solution that relieves the burden on our exhausted colleagues without demanding a level of coordination that they cannot provide. Simplicity is often the highest form of sophistication.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Servas is right. If we choose a project that uses fixed fees instead of per-head licenses, it might be easier to manage. I'm just scared that we'll commit to something now and then find out next year that we can't afford the renewal.","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, don't worry so much! We'll find a way! But @Asuka, if the coordination group is so tired, maybe we should pick something that doesn't need them to do more work? And it definitely can't need the developers!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, that is a logical conclusion. We must avoid any proposal that relies on the already overextended developers or the coordination group. The priority should be a tool that automates the redundant data entry I discovered.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, automation is only a solution if the implementation doesn't create a new administrative nightmare. If the rollout requires manual oversight from the coordination group, we are simply trading one form of exhaustion for another. We need a low-maintenance tool.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"We have spoken with great honesty. It appears we seek a rare specimen: a tool that is narrow in scope yet deep in utility, requiring neither the developers' time nor the coordination group's strength to survive. Let us carry this mindfulness into the final round.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I hope we can find something like that. I'll be looking for a project that doesn't rely on the frozen capital budget and has predictable costs, so we don't have any scary surprises next year.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"I'll be looking for a project that doesn't need the internet at the plants or the busy developers! We need something that just works, even if the signal goes poof! I'm ready for the candidates! Yay!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will be looking for a candidate that directly addresses the documented waste of time and the data conflicts I found. A project that sounds impressive but ignores these daily losses is a failure.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I will be looking for a candidate that requires minimal administrative overhead. We must prioritize a solution that provides immediate relief to our staff rather than one that adds to their existing, unsustainable workload.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
