64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Looking at our candidates, the Supplier Data Hub seems most harmonious. It aligns with my finding that narrow, trade-specific tools endure, and it directly addresses the data conflicts and redundant copying Ryuji discovered.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I think the Supplier Data Hub could work. It seems like it would use a fixed-fee setup for the catalog rather than per-head licenses, which would be safer since our capital budget is frozen.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Wait! The Field Service App sounds super cool, but it's a trap! I found out the plants have no signal and getting devices approved takes forever! It would be a total disaster! The Supplier Data Hub is way safer!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. The Supplier Data Hub is the only candidate that directly solves the systemic waste I identified. It eliminates the daily hours lost to copying records and resolves the conflicting address data causing misrouted deliveries.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"The Supplier Data Hub is the most logical choice. By consolidating records, it eliminates the redundant requests my findings revealed and reduces the manual burden on the coordination group. It provides relief without adding new administrative complexity.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"It is a rare and beautiful thing when we find such complete alignment. We have looked into the past and the present, and the Supplier Data Hub emerges as the path that honors both our resources and our people.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I feel much better now that we all agree. If the Supplier Data Hub uses a stable cost model, it won't put us in a difficult position when the renewal comes next year. I'm happy to support it.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"I'm so happy we all agree! The Supplier Data Hub is like a big, organized treasure chest for everyone to share! Plus, it doesn't need the busy developers or the disappearing internet. It's the perfect choice! Yay!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,The logic is consistent. The other options are either irrelevant to our daily losses or introduce risks we cannot afford. The Supplier Data Hub is the only proposal grounded in the reality of our operational failures.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"I concur. The other candidates, particularly the Workflow Assistant, would likely place an undue burden on the already exhausted coordination group. The Supplier Data Hub is the only option that reduces the workload rather than redistributing it.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"We have walked this path together with patience and clarity. By choosing a tool that is focused and sustainable, we ensure that our innovation serves the workers rather than becoming another burden for them to carry.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm glad we could find a solution that everyone likes. It feels safe to go with the Supplier Data Hub, and I think it's the most responsible way to use the software allowance we have left.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Sakura,,I'm just so glad we're not picking the app! Imagine the technicians' faces when their tablets don't work and they can't get them approved! The Supplier Data Hub is a winner! I vote for the Supplier Data Hub!,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I have no reason to deviate. The Supplier Data Hub is the only candidate that addresses the documented waste of time and the data conflicts on the floor. I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. The Supplier Data Hub is the only proposal that actively reduces the manual, redundant work currently crushing our skeleton crew. It is the most responsible choice for our staff. I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It has been a privilege to deliberate with you all. In our unity, we have found a path that honors both the science of our operations and the spirit of our people. I cast my vote for the Supplier Data Hub.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm really glad we could all agree on this. It feels like the safest choice for our budget and the most helpful for everyone. I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Sakura,,This was so much fun! I'm super happy we found a project that won't get stuck in a signal hole or make the developers grumpy! I vote for the Supplier Data Hub! Yay!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,The evidence is conclusive. The Supplier Data Hub is the only option that prioritizes the resolution of actual operational failures over theoretical appeal. I cast my final vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Asuka,,The decision is based on a clear understanding of our current limitations. The Supplier Data Hub is the only option that respects our staffing constraints while eliminating redundant labor. I cast my final vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
